  <main id="main-content" role="main">
  <div class="poster">

    <!-- ===== HEADER ===== -->
    <header class="poster-header" role="banner">
      <div class="poster-header-eyebrow animate">Systematic Review · Foundation Models in Healthcare</div>
      <h1 class="animate delay-1">Large Language Models in Medicine:<br>Opportunities, Risks, and the Path Forward</h1>
      <p class="poster-header-subtitle animate delay-2">
        A comprehensive review of how large language models are transforming clinical practice, medical research, and healthcare delivery — along with the critical challenges that must be addressed for safe deployment.
      </p>
      <div class="poster-header-meta animate delay-3">
        <span class="meta-badge source">Nature Medicine · July 2023</span>
        <span class="meta-badge">Medical AI &amp; Digital Health Conference 2024</span>
        <span class="meta-badge">Systematic Review</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- ===== METRICS BAND ===== -->
    <section class="metrics-band" aria-label="Key metrics">
      <div class="metrics-label">Key Figures at a Glance</div>
      <div class="metrics-grid">
        <div class="metric-card animate delay-1">
          <div class="metric-value" data-count="90" data-prefix=">" data-suffix="%">>90%</div>
          <div class="metric-label">GPT-4 USMLE Score</div>
          <div class="metric-context">Exceeded the ~60% passing threshold on all three USMLE licensing exam steps</div>
        </div>
        <div class="metric-card animate delay-2">
          <div class="metric-value" data-count="500" data-prefix="" data-suffix="+">500+</div>
          <div class="metric-label">PubMed Articles (2023)</div>
          <div class="metric-context">Peer-reviewed publications on LLMs in medicine published in 2023 alone</div>
        </div>
        <div class="metric-card risk-card animate delay-3">
          <div class="metric-value">Up to 30%</div>
          <div class="metric-label">Hallucination Rate</div>
          <div class="metric-context">Studies report fabricated medical references or inaccurate clinical information in up to 30% of outputs</div>
        </div>
        <div class="metric-card animate delay-4">
          <div class="metric-value">$10.5B</div>
          <div class="metric-label">Global LLM Health Market 2030</div>
          <div class="metric-context">Projected market size for healthcare LLM applications by 2030</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- TENSION CALLOUT -->
      <div class="tension-banner animate delay-5" role="note" aria-label="Key tension: high USMLE scores vs high hallucination rates">
        <div class="tension-stat good">
          <span>&gt;90%</span>
          USMLE Score
        </div>
        <div class="tension-vs">vs</div>
        <div class="tension-caption">
          The central tension in medical AI: benchmark performance far exceeds what safety evidence currently justifies for clinical deployment.
        </div>
        <div class="tension-vs">vs</div>
        <div class="tension-stat bad">
          <span>~30%</span>
          Hallucination Rate
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===== MAIN CONTENT GRID ===== -->
    <div class="content-area">

      <!-- ===== OVERVIEW ===== -->
      <section class="overview-section" aria-labelledby="overview-heading">
        <div class="section-label">01 · Background</div>
        <h2 id="overview-heading" style="font-size:1.1rem; margin-bottom:0;">What Are LLMs and Why Do They Matter for Medicine?</h2>
        <div class="overview-inner">
          <div class="overview-card animate delay-1" data-reveal>
            <h3>Foundation Models</h3>
            <p>LLMs such as GPT-4, Med-PaLM 2, and LLaMA are trained on vast text corpora, enabling them to understand and generate medical language with remarkable fluency across clinical domains.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="overview-card animate delay-2" data-reveal>
            <h3>Rapid Emergence</h3>
            <p>Over 500 peer-reviewed publications appeared in 2023 alone. Health systems are integrating LLM-powered assistants into EHRs, with the global healthcare LLM market projected at $10.5B by 2030.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="overview-card animate delay-3" data-reveal>
            <h3>Scope of Impact</h3>
            <p>Foundation models are poised to reshape clinical practice, biomedical research, and medical education — from automated documentation to hypothesis generation and patient communication.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ===== APPLICATIONS ===== -->
      <section class="applications-section" aria-labelledby="apps-heading" data-reveal>
        <div class="section-label">02 · Applications</div>
        <h2 id="apps-heading" style="font-size:1.1rem; margin-bottom:0;">Key Clinical &amp; Research Applications</h2>
        <table class="app-table" aria-label="Clinical application areas and maturity stages">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Application Area</th>
              <th>Example Use Cases</th>
              <th style="text-align:center;">Maturity</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><span class="app-area">Clinical Documentation</span></td>
              <td><span class="app-desc">Automated note generation, discharge summaries</span></td>
              <td style="text-align:center;"><span class="maturity-badge maturity-pilot">Pilot</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><span class="app-area">Diagnostic Support</span></td>
              <td><span class="app-desc">Differential diagnosis, radiology interpretation</span></td>
              <td style="text-align:center;"><span class="maturity-badge maturity-research">Research</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><span class="app-area">Patient Communication</span></td>
              <td><span class="app-desc">Answering questions, simplifying medical jargon</span></td>
              <td style="text-align:center;"><span class="maturity-badge maturity-early">Early Adoption</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><span class="app-area">Medical Education</span></td>
              <td><span class="app-desc">Exam prep, case-based learning, tutoring</span></td>
              <td style="text-align:center;"><span class="maturity-badge maturity-active">Active Use</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><span class="app-area">Biomedical Research</span></td>
              <td><span class="app-desc">Literature synthesis, hypothesis generation</span></td>
              <td style="text-align:center;"><span class="maturity-badge maturity-emerging">Emerging</span></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <!-- ===== PERFORMANCE ===== -->
      <section class="performance-section" aria-labelledby="perf-heading" data-reveal>
        <div class="section-label">03 · Evidence</div>
        <h2 id="perf-heading" style="font-size:1.1rem; margin-bottom:0;">Performance Benchmarks</h2>
        <div class="benchmark-list">
          <div class="benchmark-item">
            <div class="benchmark-header">
              <div>
                <div class="benchmark-model">GPT-4</div>
                <div class="benchmark-note" style="margin-top:2px;">USMLE Steps 1, 2 &amp; 3 · OpenAI, 2023</div>
              </div>
              <div class="benchmark-score score-high">&gt;90%</div>
            </div>
            <div class="benchmark-bar-wrap">
              <div class="benchmark-bar bar-high" style="width: 91%;"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="benchmark-note">Substantially exceeded the ~60% passing threshold on all three steps</div>
          </div>
          <div class="benchmark-item">
            <div class="benchmark-header">
              <div>
                <div class="benchmark-model">Med-PaLM 2</div>
                <div class="benchmark-note" style="margin-top:2px;">MedQA Benchmark · Google, 2023</div>
              </div>
              <div class="benchmark-score score-high">86.5%</div>
            </div>
            <div class="benchmark-bar-wrap">
              <div class="benchmark-bar bar-med-high" style="width: 86%;"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="benchmark-note">Approaching expert physician-level performance on standardized medical QA</div>
          </div>
          <div class="benchmark-item">
            <div class="benchmark-header">
              <div>
                <div class="benchmark-model">GPT-3.5</div>
                <div class="benchmark-note" style="margin-top:2px;">USMLE · OpenAI, 2022</div>
              </div>
              <div class="benchmark-score score-mid">~60%</div>
            </div>
            <div class="benchmark-bar-wrap">
              <div class="benchmark-bar bar-pass" style="width: 60%;"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="benchmark-note">Near passing threshold; limited on complex clinical reasoning tasks</div>
          </div>
          <div class="passing-line">
            <strong>Passing threshold: ~60%</strong> — LLMs encode substantial medical knowledge, though performance on real-world clinical scenarios remains less characterized.
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ===== RISKS ===== -->
      <section class="risks-section" aria-labelledby="risks-heading" data-reveal>
        <div class="section-label risk">04 · Risks &amp; Limitations</div>
        <h2 id="risks-heading" style="font-size:1.1rem; margin-bottom:0;">Critical Challenges &amp; Ethical Concerns</h2>
        <div class="risks-inner">

          <div class="risk-item">
            <div class="risk-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#e8913a" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M10.29 3.86L1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0z"/><line x1="12" y1="9" x2="12" y2="13"/><line x1="12" y1="17" x2="12.01" y2="17"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div class="risk-content">
              <div class="risk-title">Hallucinations</div>
              <div class="risk-desc">LLMs can fabricate plausible-sounding but incorrect medical information, including fake citations and erroneous clinical guidance.</div>
              <span class="risk-highlight">Up to 30% fabrication rate in medical Q&amp;A tasks</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="risk-item">
            <div class="risk-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#e8913a" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M17 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M23 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div class="risk-content">
              <div class="risk-title">Bias &amp; Health Equity</div>
              <div class="risk-desc">Models may perpetuate or amplify biases present in training data, leading to care disparities across demographic groups.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="risk-item">
            <div class="risk-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#e8913a" stroke-width="2.5"><rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2" ry="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div class="risk-content">
              <div class="risk-title">Privacy &amp; Data Security</div>
              <div class="risk-desc">Patient data used in prompts may be transmitted to external servers, raising serious HIPAA and GDPR compliance concerns.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="risk-item">
            <div class="risk-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#e8913a" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M9 11l3 3L22 4"/><path d="M21 12v7a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h11"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div class="risk-content">
              <div class="risk-title">Lack of Clinical Validation</div>
              <div class="risk-desc">Most LLM evaluations rely on multiple-choice benchmarks rather than prospective clinical trials in real-world settings.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="risk-item">
            <div class="risk-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#e8913a" stroke-width="2.5"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 8v4"/><path d="M12 16h.01"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div class="risk-content">
              <div class="risk-title">Over-reliance &amp; Automation Bias</div>
              <div class="risk-desc">Clinicians may develop automation bias, accepting LLM outputs without sufficient critical appraisal or independent verification.</div>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ===== BENCHMARK CHART ===== -->
      <section class="chart-section" aria-labelledby="chart-heading" data-reveal>
        <div class="section-label">Performance vs Risk — The Core Tension</div>
        <h2 id="chart-heading" style="font-size:1.0rem; font-weight:600; color:var(--text-secondary);">Model benchmark scores (USMLE/MedQA %) alongside reported hallucination rate — illustrating the gap between capability and safety</h2>
        <div role="img" aria-label="Bar chart comparing GPT-4, Med-PaLM 2, and GPT-3.5 USMLE scores with the LLM hallucination rate, showing high benchmark performance contrasting with significant hallucination risk">
          <div class="chart-container">
            <canvas id="benchmarkChart" role="img" aria-label="Benchmark performance vs hallucination risk comparison chart"></canvas>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ===== FRAMEWORK ===== -->
      <section class="framework-section" aria-labelledby="framework-heading" data-reveal>
        <div class="section-label">05 · Responsible Deployment</div>
        <div class="framework-title" id="framework-heading">A Framework for Safe Clinical Integration</div>
        <div class="framework-steps">
          <div class="framework-step">
            <div class="step-num">01 · Evaluation</div>
            <div class="step-title">Rigorous Prospective Trials</div>
            <div class="step-desc">Test in diverse clinical settings before deployment. Benchmark performance is necessary but not sufficient.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="framework-step">
            <div class="step-num">02 · Oversight</div>
            <div class="step-title">Human-in-the-Loop Design</div>
            <div class="step-desc">Ensure clinician oversight of all LLM-generated outputs. No autonomous clinical decisions.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="framework-step">
            <div class="step-num">03 · Transparency</div>
            <div class="step-title">Open Reporting</div>
            <div class="step-desc">Disclose model limitations, training data sources, and known failure modes to clinical users.</div>
          </div>
